<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">gathering</ansi>

Out in the wild your company can work for its supplies instead of only
buying them. A room that offers herbs, firewood, fishing or game says so on
the "Here:" line when you <ansi fg="command">look</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help resources</ansi>); the commands below do the work.
Gathering takes real time and effort, can draw trouble, and strips a room
for a while. It never advances the game clock.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The commands</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">gather</ansi>
  Lists what the room offers, how much is left, and what you can do.

  <ansi fg="command">gather herbs</ansi>      20 s   herbs                             needs: nothing
  <ansi fg="command">gather firewood</ansi>   20 s   2 firewood bundles                needs: nothing
  <ansi fg="command">fish</ansi>              30 s   0 to 2 fish                       needs: a fishing line
  <ansi fg="command">hunt</ansi>              30 s   raw game meat, now and then a hide   needs: nothing

Only the leader of the company gives the order. The whole company takes
part, so companions standing with you add to the haul. Any other command
than <ansi fg="command">look</ansi> or <ansi fg="command">conditions</ansi>, moving, an attack, or a fight cancels the work with
nothing gained. You can't start in battle, while resting or while travelling.

While the work runs, <ansi fg="command">status</ansi> and the prompt show it on the Doing line ("Gathering
herbs 40%, 12s left"). In the web client the Room Info window shows a bar
that fills over the work's length, then what the company brought back (or
that the work was stopped).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What you find</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Herbs</ansi>  1 to 2, such as wild thyme and mushrooms. A ranger (Forage,
  <ansi fg="command">help forage</ansi>) adds one for every 2 levels, a bladed weapon in the company
  adds one, and a Scribe may find one rarer herb. In darkness the haul is
  halved. With no ranger present, 15 gathers in 100 return a worthless
  bitter weed instead: telling good leaves from bad is a skill.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Firewood</ansi>  2 bundles. A hatchet or axe (a cleaving weapon in the
  company) doubles that, and a warrior's Field Smith skill adds one. In rain
  or a storm half the bundles come back damp.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Fish</ansi>  Two chances at 40 in 100 each, better with a ranger. The line
  breaks now and then (5 in 100) and is lost. Fishing needs a room marked
  fishing, or fresh water on a shore. Buy a fishing line at a market or
  from the old fisherman at Frost Lake.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Game</ansi>  Half the hunts bring something down; a ranger adds 5 points
  for each level, up to 90. A bow, crossbow or sling in the company is the
  way to hunt. Without one the company sets snares instead and keeps only
  half the chance. A kill brings 2 raw game meat (3 with a ranger) and,
  about one time in three, a hide or a pelt. Hunting is noisy: it adds 10
  to the chance that a random encounter finds you (<ansi fg="command">help encounters</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Effort and danger</ansi>

Every attempt costs the whole company the Fatigue of one step on that
ground (half for fishing; <ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>). Each attempt also rolls the
zone's random encounter chance once, so a long stay in dangerous country
draws a fight.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Picked clean</ansi>

Each room holds only so much: 3 herb gathers, 4 firewood gathers, 4 fishing
attempts and 2 hunts. Every attempt that finishes spends one, even a fishing
cast that catches nothing. One comes back every 20 minutes of real time
(40 for game), and a restart never refills them early. The stock belongs to
the room, so every company shares it: whoever arrives first takes the
bounty. <ansi fg="command">look</ansi> adds "(picked clean)" after what is gone, and the web
client's map draws that marker hollow with a slash.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Firewood and the camp fire</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">camp fire</ansi> needs fuel. In a room that offers firewood the deadfall feeds the
fire for nothing. Anywhere else it burns one firewood bundle from your pack,
a companion's pack or the cargo. A damp bundle lights only on a second try
and the smoky fire it makes gives no warmth. With no firewood you cannot
light the fire, so you cannot rest at camp (an inn is not affected). Markets
sell bundles but never buy them back: prepare before you set out, and
<ansi fg="command">camp status</ansi> shows the fuel your company carries (<ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>). One
bundle fuels one rest: a finished rest leaves embers, and the next one needs
the fire fed again. Fire steel and tinder light damp wood first time with
full warmth (<ansi fg="command">help camp gear</ansi>).

Gathered fish is cooked into grilled fish (<ansi fg="command">help cooking</ansi>); herbs, meat and
hides feed cooks, markets and the trades.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help resources</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help forage</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cooking</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help survival</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>.
